)
select b.id, s.id, v.code, v.name, v.slug, v.glaze_type, v.base_color, v.swatch, v.family, v.tags, v.finish,
       v.opacity, v.cmin::smallint, v.cmax::smallint, v.food::boolean, v.notes, v.url, v.app,
       v.coats_min::smallint, v.coats_max::smallint, v.image, v.credit
from (values
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-classic$v$, $v$SW-464$v$, $v$Blue Moon Rocks$v$, $v$mayco-blue-moon-rocks$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Blue dimensional, puffed texture in varying sizes$v$, $v$#8b98b9$v$, $v$blue$v$, array[$v$blue$v$]::text[], null, null, 5, 10, false, $v$Cone 6 oxidation (larger image): Blue dimensional, puffed texture in varying sizes. Cone 10 reduction: Puffed texture may increase. Color darkens. Tips for Use: Layer Together: Moon Rocks can be layered with other Moon Rock colors to create stunning visual effects. Allow the first layer to set slightly (loses its glossiness) before adding the next. Alternate directions of coats (apply one layer vertically and the next layer horizontally). 1-2 coats of each color are recommended, but additional coats will produce a more pronounced puffed pattern. Use with Underglazes and Engobes: Moon Rocks remains dimensional when applied over Underglazes and Stoneware Engobes, preserving its raised texture. For best results, it is recommended to bisque fire the Underglaze or Engobe to cone 04 before applying the Melt Gloop, as this helps with adhesion and ensures the glaze performs effectively during the final firing. Layer with Stoneware Glazes: When used either under or over a glaze, such as Stoneware glazes, the texture may flatten during firing. Despite this change, the technique can still produce interesting and colorful effects. Firing Range: Moon Rocks have a broad firing range from cone 5 to cone 10 (2167°F-2345°F /1186°C-1285°C) in both oxidation and reduction firings. Firing at higher temperatures may result in the glaze texture to increase and colors to darken. Because results can vary based on firing conditions and layering techniques, it’s recommended to test the glaze beforehand. Dinnerware: Moon Rocks are not suitable for dinnerware due to surface texture. However, it can be used on the outside of functional ware, below the lip line.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw464-blue-moon-rocks/$v$, null, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/sw464.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-crystal$v$, $v$SW-225$v$, $v$Lily Pad$v$, $v$mayco-lily-pad$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Lily Pad is a glossy, semi-opaque white glaze that breaks over texture$v$, $v$#bab49f$v$, $v$white$v$, array[$v$white$v$,$v$green$v$]::text[], $v$gloss$v$, $v$semi-opaque$v$, 5, 10, false, $v$Cone 6: Lily Pad is a glossy, semi-opaque white glaze that breaks over texture. Contains green specks. Stable glaze. Cone 10: Lily Pad changes to a glossy blue. Heavy crystal application may effect color results and movement.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw225-lily-pad/$v$, $v$Upon opening, specks will be concentrated in the bottom of the bottle. Stir/shake thoroughly to incorporate before each use. Specks can create movement. Avoid having a heavy concentration of specks near the bottom of your piece.$v$, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/SW225-Lily-Pad.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-matte$v$, $v$SW-231$v$, $v$Lilac Speck$v$, $v$mayco-lilac-speck$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Lilac Speck is a satin-matte, semi-opaque light purple that breaks over texture$v$, $v$#d2a4b3$v$, $v$purple$v$, array[$v$purple$v$,$v$orange$v$,$v$yellow$v$]::text[], $v$satin$v$, $v$semi-opaque$v$, 5, 10, true, $v$Cone 6: Lilac Speck is a satin-matte, semi-opaque light purple that breaks over texture. Contains small purple, orange and yellow specks. Stable glaze. Cone 10: Lilac Speck lightens to off-white. Specks blur and lose definition with increased application thickness; crystallization may develop. Remains stable.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw231-lilac-speck/$v$, $v$We recommend firing our matte glazes to cone 6 to produce a satin matte finish. Upon opening, specks will be concentrated in the bottom of the bottle. Stir/shake thoroughly to incorporate before each use.$v$, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/SW231-Lilac-Speck.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-matte$v$, $v$SW-232$v$, $v$Baby Blue Speck$v$, $v$mayco-baby-blue-speck$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Baby Blue Speck is a Satin-matte, semi-opaque light blue that breaks over texture$v$, $v$#bdd3d2$v$, $v$blue$v$, array[$v$blue$v$,$v$purple$v$,$v$orange$v$,$v$yellow$v$]::text[], $v$satin$v$, $v$semi-opaque$v$, 5, 10, true, $v$Cone 6: Baby Blue Speck is a Satin-matte, semi-opaque light blue that breaks over texture. Contains small purple, orange and yellow specks. Stable glaze. Cone 10: Specks blur and lose definition with increased application thickness; crystallization may develop. Remains stable.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw232-baby-blue-speck/$v$, $v$We recommend firing our matte glazes to cone 6 to produce a satin matte finish. Upon opening, specks will be concentrated in the bottom of the bottle. Stir/shake thoroughly to incorporate before each use.$v$, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/SW232-Baby-Blue-Speck.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-classic$v$, $v$SW-465$v$, $v$Black Moon Rocks$v$, $v$mayco-black-moon-rocks$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Black dimensional, puffed texture in varying sizes$v$, $v$#5f5d5b$v$, $v$black$v$, array[$v$black$v$]::text[], null, null, 5, 10, false, $v$Cone 6 oxidation (larger image): Black dimensional, puffed texture in varying sizes. Cone 10 reduction: Puffed texture may increase. Color darkens. Tips for Use: Layer Together: Moon Rocks can be layered with other Moon Rock colors to create stunning visual effects. Allow the first layer to set slightly (loses its glossiness) before adding the next. Alternate directions of coats (apply one layer vertically and the next layer horizontally). 1-2 coats of each color are recommended, but additional coats will produce a more pronounced puffed pattern. Use with Underglazes and Engobes: Moon Rocks remains dimensional when applied over Underglazes and Stoneware Engobes, preserving its raised texture. For best results, it is recommended to bisque fire the Underglaze or Engobe to cone 04 before applying the Melt Gloop, as this helps with adhesion and ensures the glaze performs effectively during the final firing. Layer with Stoneware Glazes: When used either under or over a glaze, such as Stoneware glazes, the texture may flatten during firing. Despite this change, the technique can still produce interesting and colorful effects. Firing Range: Moon Rocks have a broad firing range from cone 5 to cone 10 (2167°F-2345°F /1186°C-1285°C) in both oxidation and reduction firings. Firing at higher temperatures may result in the glaze texture to increase and colors to darken. Because results can vary based on firing conditions and layering techniques, it’s recommended to test the glaze beforehand. Dinnerware: Moon Rocks are not suitable for dinnerware due to surface texture. However, it can be used on the outside of functional ware, below the lip line.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw465-black-moon-rocks/$v$, null, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/sw465.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-classic$v$, $v$SW-100$v$, $v$Blue Surf$v$, $v$mayco-blue-surf$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Blue Surf is a variegated cobalt blue glazes that breaks green$v$, $v$#202f47$v$, $v$blue$v$, array[$v$blue$v$,$v$green$v$]::text[], null, null, 5, 10, true, $v$Cone 6: Blue Surf is a variegated cobalt blue glazes that breaks green. Cone 10: Color darkens.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw-100-blue-surf/$v$, $v$The thinner the application the the more green the glaze will appear. The thicker the more blue it will be. Where the glaze breaks it will be green.$v$, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/sw-100.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-classic$v$, $v$SW-101$v$, $v$Stoned Denim$v$, $v$mayco-stoned-denim$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Stoned Denim is a variegated blue glaze that breaks brown$v$, $v$#60767f$v$, $v$blue$v$, array[$v$blue$v$,$v$brown$v$]::text[], null, null, 5, 10, true, $v$Cone 6 oxidation (larger image): Stoned Denim is a variegated blue glaze that breaks brown. Cone 10 reduction (smaller image): Color darkens.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw-101-stoned-denim/$v$, $v$The thinner the application the more brown the glaze will be. The thicker the application, the more blue the glaze will be. Where the glaze breaks it will be brown.$v$, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/10/SW-101-Stoned-Denim-1024x1024.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-matte$v$, $v$SW-104$v$, $v$Black Walnut$v$, $v$mayco-black-walnut$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Black Walnut is a dark brown soft matte glaze that breaks a rich warm brown$v$, $v$#241b16$v$, $v$black$v$, array[$v$black$v$,$v$brown$v$]::text[], $v$matte$v$, null, 5, 10, true, $v$Cone 6 oxidation (larger image): Black Walnut is a dark brown soft matte glaze that breaks a rich warm brown. Cone 10 reduction (smaller image): Rich brown undertones come through.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw-104-black-walnut/$v$, $v$The thinner the application, the lighter brown the color. The thicker the application, the darker the brown color. For a saturated opaque finish, apply 4+ coats. Has a satin finish. Wood and soda firing results will vary.$v$, 4, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/sw-104.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-matte$v$, $v$SW-105$v$, $v$Frost Blue$v$, $v$mayco-frost-blue$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Frost Blue is a mottled blue soft matte glaze that breaks a muted green/gray$v$, $v$#586270$v$, $v$blue$v$, array[$v$blue$v$,$v$green$v$,$v$gray$v$]::text[], $v$matte$v$, null, 5, 10, true, $v$Cone 6 oxidation (larger image): Frost Blue is a mottled blue soft matte glaze that breaks a muted green/gray. Cone 10 reduction (smaller image): Semi-gloss finish with variegated blue/light blue. Can exhibit green hues.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw-105-frost-blue/$v$, $v$Because of the chemical make up, this glaze can vary between a green and blue finish. It has a satin finish. If you like the results that Robins Egg (SW116) gives you, then you will enjoy this glaze because they are made up of similar things. Wood and soda firing results will vary.$v$, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/sw-105.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-matte$v$, $v$SW-106$v$, $v$Alabaster$v$, $v$mayco-alabaster$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Alabaster is a semi-opaque white soft matte glaze that breaks over texture$v$, $v$#cec4b6$v$, $v$white$v$, array[$v$white$v$]::text[], $v$matte$v$, $v$semi-opaque$v$, 5, 10, true, $v$Cone 6: Alabaster is a semi-opaque white soft matte glaze that breaks over texture. Cone 10: Color darkens to variegated light gray/purple.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw-106-alabaster/$v$, $v$When using this glaze, you will be able to pick up the characteristics of the clay body due to it’s white semi opaque finish. Combos really well with 2 coats of stroke and coat on top. It has a satin finish. If you like combos with Sea Salt, you will get similar results with Alabaster minus the crystals. Wood and soda firing results will vary.$v$, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/10/SW-106-Alabaster-1024x1024.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-matte$v$, $v$SW-107$v$, $v$Dunes$v$, $v$mayco-dunes$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Dunes is a semi-opaque off-white soft matte glaze that breaks over texture$v$, $v$#8e867b$v$, $v$white$v$, array[$v$white$v$]::text[], $v$matte$v$, $v$semi-opaque$v$, 5, 10, true, $v$Cone 6: Dunes is a semi-opaque off-white soft matte glaze that breaks over texture. Cone 10: Color darkens to variegated gray.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw-107-dunes/$v$, $v$The lighter the application, the more brown the glaze will appear. The thicker the glaze application, the lighter tan the color.$v$, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/sw-107.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-matte$v$, $v$SW-109$v$, $v$Capri Blue$v$, $v$mayco-capri-blue$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Capri Blue is a variegated blue glaze that breaks over texture$v$, $v$#303f5a$v$, $v$blue$v$, array[$v$blue$v$]::text[], null, null, 5, 10, true, $v$Cone 6 oxidation (larger image): Capri Blue is a variegated blue glaze that breaks over texture. Cone 10 reduction (smaller image): Semi-gloss finish with variegated blue/green.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw-109-capri-blue/$v$, $v$The lighter the application the greener the glaze. The thicker the application the bluer the glaze. If you like Green Tea and oyster combos, try Capri blue because those 3 glazes are in the same glaze family. Gloss finish.$v$, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/sw-109.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-classic$v$, $v$SW-110$v$, $v$Oyster$v$, $v$mayco-oyster$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Oyster is a variegated cream/brown glaze that exhibits gray/purple undertones and breaks brown$v$, $v$#735e50$v$, $v$cream$v$, array[$v$cream$v$,$v$brown$v$,$v$gray$v$,$v$purple$v$]::text[], null, null, 5, 10, true, $v$Cone 6 oxidation (larger image): Oyster is a variegated cream/brown glaze that exhibits gray/purple undertones and breaks brown. Cone 10 reduction (smaller image): Color changes to a variegated brown/cream. Increased movement.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw-110-oyster/$v$, $v$If your kiln fires cool, the glaze finish may be brown. An iridescent finish may be achieved by re-firing or if your kiln fires hot. If you like Green Tea and Capri Blue combos, then try oyster because these three glazes are in the same glaze family.$v$, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/sw-110.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-matte$v$, $v$SW-111$v$, $v$Wrought Iron$v$, $v$mayco-wrought-iron$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Wrought Iron creates an intermittent, dappled black gloss-matte finish that is reminiscent of high fire oil-spot glazes$v$, $v$#29201d$v$, $v$black$v$, array[$v$black$v$]::text[], $v$matte$v$, null, 5, 10, true, $v$Cone 6: Wrought Iron creates an intermittent, dappled black gloss-matte finish that is reminiscent of high fire oil-spot glazes. Typically, oil-spot glazes are thickly applied and require some reduction during the firing to achieve the oil-matte effects; Wrought Iron does the job with just two coats in a cone 6 oxidation firing. Cone 10: Color changes to a dark metallic gray.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw-111-wrought-iron/$v$, $v$The thinner the application the more brown the glaze. The thicker the application the more black the glaze. This glaze is not completely matte, but will have a matte finish with variation of gloss. Due to the high manganese content, there is a chance of bubbling on a speckled clay body.$v$, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/sw-111.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-classic$v$, $v$SW-112$v$, $v$Tiger's Eye$v$, $v$mayco-tiger-s-eye$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Tiger’s Eye breaks from a glossy deep brownish-red to frothy amber depending on the application thickness$v$, $v$#453924$v$, $v$red$v$, array[$v$red$v$,$v$amber$v$]::text[], $v$gloss$v$, null, 5, 10, true, $v$Cone 6: Tiger’s Eye breaks from a glossy deep brownish-red to frothy amber depending on the application thickness. one to two coats will produce browns and reds; three to five coats will result in more glaze movement and color variation. While you’ll experience beautiful movement with Tiger’s Eye, the glaze will not run off your ware during a cone 6 oxidation firing. Cone 10: Color darkens.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw-112-tigers-eye/$v$, $v$Thinner applications will produce darker browns and reds; heavier applications will lean towards an opaque, light brown finish. Butted against another glaze, Tiger’s Eye will gently merge with it – SW-104 Black Walnut is a nice complementary glaze to use. Wood and soda firing results will vary.$v$, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/sw-112.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-classic$v$, $v$SW-113$v$, $v$Speckled Plum$v$, $v$mayco-speckled-plum$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Speckled Plum produces a reddish brown gloss finish (one to two light coats) and evolves to deliver floating maroon-mauve tones with heavier$v$, $v$#6e2e2b$v$, $v$plum$v$, array[$v$plum$v$,$v$brown$v$]::text[], $v$gloss$v$, null, 5, 10, true, $v$Cone 6 oxidation (larger image): Speckled Plum produces a reddish brown gloss finish (one to two light coats) and evolves to deliver floating maroon-mauve tones with heavier applications (three to four coats). Heavier applications may also yield bands of reddish-mauve specks when used with certain clay bodies. While you’ll enjoy how Speckled Plum moves, the glaze will not run off your ware during a cone 6 oxidation firing. Cone 10 reduction (smaller image): Color darkens.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw-113-speckled-plum/$v$, $v$Thinner applications will produce darker browns and reds; heavier applications will begin to show an opaque, maroon-mauve float.$v$, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/sw-113.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-crystal$v$, $v$SW-115$v$, $v$Midnight Rain$v$, $v$mayco-midnight-rain$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Midnight Rain is a blue-green breaking gloss glaze that contains a black crystal$v$, $v$#223339$v$, $v$blue$v$, array[$v$blue$v$,$v$green$v$,$v$black$v$]::text[], $v$gloss$v$, null, 5, 10, true, $v$Cone 6 oxidation (larger image): Midnight Rain is a blue-green breaking gloss glaze that contains a black crystal. As the crystal melts and moves, a black oil-like streak is created in the glaze. Cone 10 reduction (smaller image): Crystals melt and integrate into base glaze, darkening the color. Increased movement.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw-115-midnight-rain/$v$, $v$SW-100 Blue Surf is the base glaze. For a lighter crystal effect, you may try applying two coats of SW-100 Blue Surf with a third coat of SW-115 Midnight Rain. Wood and soda firing results will vary.$v$, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/sw-115.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-crystal$v$, $v$SW-116$v$, $v$Robin's Egg$v$, $v$mayco-robin-s-egg$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Robin’s Egg is a greenish-blue matte glaze that contains a sand-colored crystal$v$, $v$#777e7f$v$, $v$blue$v$, array[$v$blue$v$,$v$brown$v$]::text[], $v$matte$v$, null, 5, 10, true, $v$Cone 6 oxidation (larger image): Robin’s Egg is a greenish-blue matte glaze that contains a sand-colored crystal. As the crystal melts, a small sandy-brown bloom will appear in the glaze, producing a mottled, textured finish. Cone 10 reduction (smaller image): Semi-gloss finish with variegated blue/light blue and crystals.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw-116-robins-egg/$v$, $v$SW-105 Frost Blue is the base glaze. For a lighter crystal effect, you may try applying two coats of SW-105 Frost Blue with a third coat of SW-116 Robin’s Egg. Wood and soda firing results will vary.$v$, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/sw-116.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-crystal$v$, $v$SW-117$v$, $v$Honeycomb$v$, $v$mayco-honeycomb$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Honeycomb is a variegated brown matte glaze that contains a sandy-brown crystal$v$, $v$#8d7550$v$, $v$brown$v$, array[$v$brown$v$,$v$yellow$v$]::text[], $v$matte$v$, null, 5, 10, true, $v$Cone 6: Honeycomb is a variegated brown matte glaze that contains a sandy-brown crystal. As the crystal melts it creates glossy blooms that can produce yellow mottling in the glaze, producing a textured fired finish. Cone 10: Color darkens.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw-117-honeycomb/$v$, $v$SW-103 Sisal is the base glaze. For a lighter crystal effect, you may try applying two coats of SW-103 Sisal with a third coat of SW-117 Honeycomb.$v$, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/sw-117.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-crystal$v$, $v$SW-118$v$, $v$Sea Salt$v$, $v$mayco-sea-salt$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Sea Salt is a white matte glaze that contains a sage green crystal$v$, $v$#cfc5b2$v$, $v$white$v$, array[$v$white$v$,$v$sage$v$,$v$green$v$]::text[], $v$matte$v$, null, 5, 10, true, $v$Cone 6: Sea Salt is a white matte glaze that contains a sage green crystal. As the crystal melts, green blooms appear in the glaze, producing a foamy, textured fired finish. Cone 10: Base glaze turns pale lavender/gray. Crystals are mint green.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw-118-sea-salt/$v$, $v$SW-106 Alabaster is the base glaze. For a lighter crystal effect, you may try applying two coats of SW-106 Alabaster with a third coat of SW-118 Sea Salt.$v$, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/10/SW-118-Sea-Salt.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-classic$v$, $v$SW-119$v$, $v$Cinnabar$v$, $v$mayco-cinnabar$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Cinnabar is a rich maroon-red gloss glaze that tends to develop a hazy purple float with heavier application$v$, $v$#581413$v$, $v$red$v$, array[$v$red$v$,$v$purple$v$]::text[], $v$gloss$v$, null, 5, 10, true, $v$Cone 6: Cinnabar is a rich maroon-red gloss glaze that tends to develop a hazy purple float with heavier application. Cone 10: Color darkens.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw-119-cinnabar/$v$, $v$One to two coats will produce an opaque maroon-red; three+ coats will produce higher levels of purple float. You’ll produce beautiful color variations with Cinnabar without the glaze running off your ware during a cone 6 oxidation firing.$v$, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/sw-119.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-classic$v$, $v$SW-120$v$, $v$Northern Woods$v$, $v$mayco-northern-woods$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Northern Woods is a semi-transparent bluish-green glaze$v$, $v$#2c3122$v$, $v$green$v$, array[$v$green$v$,$v$brown$v$]::text[], null, $v$translucent$v$, 5, 10, true, $v$Cone 6 oxidation (larger image): Northern Woods is a semi-transparent bluish-green glaze. Lighter applications will produce a light translucent green with brown hues. As additional coats are applied the green hues will deepen and develop a bluish tint. Very nice on white stoneware and porcelain. Cone 10 reduction (smaller image): No Change$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw-120-northern-woods/$v$, $v$This glaze breaks brown and when applied thin the color will be brown. Apply three heavy coats to get the deep green color.$v$, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/sw-120.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-classic$v$, $v$SW-121$v$, $v$Smoke$v$, $v$mayco-smoke$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Smoke is an opaque grey-blue stoneware glaze with soft, subtle variegating hues$v$, $v$#4c4a3c$v$, $v$gray$v$, array[$v$gray$v$,$v$blue$v$]::text[], null, $v$opaque$v$, 5, 10, true, $v$Cone 6 oxidation (larger image): Smoke is an opaque grey-blue stoneware glaze with soft, subtle variegating hues. Application thickness strongly influences the fired color; surface texture will also produce variegation during the firing. Cone 10 reduction (smaller image): Color changes to a variegated sage green with a glossy finish.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw-121-smoke/$v$, $v$One coat creates a blue-grey haze over a weathered brown; Two coats intensify the grey cast while Three coats intensify the overall grey-blue opaque finish. Brown breaks on raised surfaces on the body.$v$, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/sw-121.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-classic$v$, $v$SW-122$v$, $v$Maycoshino$v$, $v$mayco-maycoshino$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Maycoshino is a variegating iron glaze with subtle color changes$v$, $v$#7b563a$v$, null, '{}'::text[], null, null, 5, 10, true, $v$Cone 6 oxidation (larger image): Maycoshino is a variegating iron glaze with subtle color changes. In a thin application, the user will achieve rich, iron browns. Applied thicker, the user will get lighter, creamy hues that are reminiscent of traditional Japanese Shino glazes. This glaze is wonderful on any surface, any color clay body. Cone 10 reduction (smaller image): Color darkens to a gray/brown.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw-122-maycoshino/$v$, $v$One coat produces a solid reddish brown opaque covering; Two coats produces a cream-tan-buff finish that breaks brown over surface texture; Three coats significantly introduces waves of cream-tan color over the reddish brown base.$v$, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/sw-122.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-classic$v$, $v$SW-123$v$, $v$Sapphire$v$, $v$mayco-sapphire$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Sapphire is a rich, deep cobalt blue glaze$v$, $v$#1a183b$v$, $v$blue$v$, array[$v$blue$v$,$v$purple$v$]::text[], $v$gloss$v$, null, 5, 10, true, $v$Cone 6: Sapphire is a rich, deep cobalt blue glaze. It has a glossy, mirrored surface which can give colors from dark blue to bluish-purple, depending upon the thickness of application. Cone 10: No Change.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw-123-sapphire/$v$, $v$If the application is too thin, the glaze will be streaky.$v$, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/sw-123.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-classic$v$, $v$SW-127$v$, $v$Olivine$v$, $v$mayco-olivine$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Olivine has rusts and several shades of green flow from this mobile gloss glaze$v$, $v$#705439$v$, $v$green$v$, array[$v$green$v$]::text[], $v$metallic$v$, null, 5, 10, true, $v$Cone 6 oxidation (larger image): Olivine has rusts and several shades of green flow from this mobile gloss glaze. Lighter coats produce muted greens and browns, 3 coats can produce a beautiful metallic green, almost mirror-like, luster. Cone 10 reduction (smaller image): Color flattens and warm undertones come through.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw-127-olivine/$v$, $v$The thinner the application, the more green the glaze will be. The thicker the application, the more brown the glaze will be. If the glaze is fired cooler, the deeper brown and less variation will appear. If too brown, put back in the kiln and fire again.$v$, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/sw-127.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-classic$v$, $v$SW-128$v$, $v$Cordovan$v$, $v$mayco-cordovan$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Cordovan develops a deep, burgundy red color with a semi-gloss surface when fired to$v$, $v$#301718$v$, $v$burgundy$v$, array[$v$burgundy$v$,$v$red$v$]::text[], $v$gloss$v$, null, 5, 10, true, $v$Cone 6 oxidation (larger image): Cordovan develops a deep, burgundy red color with a semi-gloss surface when fired to cone 5 or 6. Cordovan produces a brick or iron red on white and red midrange clay bodies. Cone 10 reduction (smaller image): Color changes to a dark metallic gray with copper/black mottling.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw-128-cordovan/$v$, $v$Two coats should be plenty to get deep red, opaque coverage; light glazers may need to add a third coat.$v$, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/sw-128.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-classic$v$, $v$SW-129$v$, $v$Copper Float$v$, $v$mayco-copper-float$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Copper Float glaze is a rich and complex midrange glaze with hues varying from reds, to coppers to gun metal blacks$v$, $v$#4f3128$v$, $v$bronze$v$, array[$v$bronze$v$,$v$red$v$]::text[], $v$satin$v$, null, 5, 10, true, $v$Cone 6: Copper Float glaze is a rich and complex midrange glaze with hues varying from reds, to coppers to gun metal blacks. Predominate coloration is a dark rusty red. The surface is satin-matte when fired to cone 5 or 6. Cone 10: Finish flattens. Color changes to a warm brown with some copper mottling.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw-129-copper-float/$v$, $v$One coat will produce dark, greenish tones, thicker coats will add greens. Thickest applications will result in metallic red hues. Wood and soda firing results will vary.$v$, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/sw-129.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-classic$v$, $v$SW-130$v$, $v$Copper Jade$v$, $v$mayco-copper-jade$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Copper Jade fires to a gloss finish, producing colors that can range from brown-greens to creamy tan hues$v$, $v$#563418$v$, $v$bronze$v$, array[$v$bronze$v$,$v$brown$v$,$v$tan$v$,$v$red$v$]::text[], $v$gloss$v$, null, 5, 10, true, $v$Cone 6: Copper Jade fires to a gloss finish, producing colors that can range from brown-greens to creamy tan hues. Color breaks dark and can pool into red tones where thick. This glaze yields complex surfaces through movement and color variation. Cone 10: Color changes to a red/brown with some black/copper mottling.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw-130-copper-jade/$v$, $v$One coat will produce dark, greenish tones, thicker coats will add greens. Thickest applications will result in metallic red hues. Liquid may have a sandy texture from jar; do not strain, the texture will fire out.$v$, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/sw-130.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-classic$v$, $v$SW-131$v$, $v$Birch$v$, $v$mayco-birch$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Birch is a creamy opaque off-white glaze that breaks brown$v$, $v$#9a8467$v$, $v$white$v$, array[$v$white$v$,$v$brown$v$]::text[], null, $v$opaque$v$, 5, 10, true, $v$Cone 6 oxidation (larger image): Birch is a creamy opaque off-white glaze that breaks brown. Cone 10 reduction (smaller image): Cream color remains and brown undertones darken.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw-131-birch/$v$, $v$The thinner the the application, the more amber the glaze will be. The thicker the application, the more white floating you will get.$v$, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/sw-131.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-classic$v$, $v$SW-132$v$, $v$Mirror Black$v$, $v$mayco-mirror-black$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Mirror Black creates a highly reflective, metallic black gloss finish$v$, $v$#2f2b24$v$, $v$black$v$, array[$v$black$v$]::text[], $v$metallic$v$, null, 5, 10, false, $v$Cone 6 oxidation (larger image): Mirror Black creates a highly reflective, metallic black gloss finish. On some vertical surfaces and around surface textures, minor matte effects can be seen; all other applications result in the formation of a black, metallic mirror. Cone 10 reduction (smaller image): Finish flattens. Color remains. Increased movement.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw-132-mirror-black/$v$, $v$This glaze WILL move. Take care when using on vertical pieces – reduce glaze thickness towards the bottom third to minimize run-off. Note: Not recommended for dinnerware due to surface durability.$v$, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/12/sw-132.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-classic$v$, $v$SW-133$v$, $v$Copper Ore$v$, $v$mayco-copper-ore$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Copper Ore is a highly mobile, reddish brown metallic glaze$v$, $v$#3d2b21$v$, $v$bronze$v$, array[$v$bronze$v$,$v$brown$v$,$v$red$v$]::text[], $v$metallic$v$, null, 5, 10, true, $v$Cone 6 oxidation (larger image): Copper Ore is a highly mobile, reddish brown metallic glaze. A dark bronze field breaks with areas of darker coloring and flashes of brighter red metallic. The movement within this glaze produces striking visual textures. Cone 10 reduction (smaller image): Finish flattens. Color turns to red/brown. Increased movement.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw-133-copper-ore/$v$, $v$This glaze WILL move. Take care when using on vertical pieces – reduce glaze thickness towards the bottom third to minimize run-off.$v$, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/sw-133.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-classic$v$, $v$SW-134$v$, $v$Eggplant$v$, $v$mayco-eggplant$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Eggplant is an opaque, gloss purple glaze$v$, $v$#2f1520$v$, $v$purple$v$, array[$v$purple$v$,$v$blue$v$,$v$gray$v$]::text[], $v$gloss$v$, $v$opaque$v$, 5, 10, true, $v$Cone 6: Eggplant is an opaque, gloss purple glaze. Three coats will create a solid purple finish. Thinner applications may result in the development of blue-gray coloring. Blue-gray colors may also develop where the glaze breaks over and around surface textures. Cone 10: Color changes to blue.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw-134-eggplant/$v$, $v$A light blue can form on top of Eggplant where it pools; surface textures also encourage the glaze to break blue. It is beautiful used in combination with other glazes.$v$, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/sw-134.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-matte$v$, $v$SW-135$v$, $v$Wintergreen$v$, $v$mayco-wintergreen$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Wintergreen is a light-green, semi-opaque satin matte glaze at$v$, $v$#95a58d$v$, $v$green$v$, array[$v$green$v$]::text[], $v$satin$v$, $v$semi-opaque$v$, 5, 10, true, $v$Cone 6: Wintergreen is a light-green, semi-opaque satin matte glaze at cone 6. Lighter coatings will allow body characteristics to appear through the glaze (especially on dark and speckled clay bodies). Use three coats to achieve the deepest opacity. Cone 10: Changes to a transparent pale green gloss with matte crystal growth.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw-135-wintergreen/$v$, $v$This is a true matte glaze at cone 5, becomes satin at cone 6.$v$, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/sw-135.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-matte$v$, $v$SW-136$v$, $v$Weathered Blue$v$, $v$mayco-weathered-blue$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Weathered Blue is designed to produce a blue to white variegation depending on the application$v$, $v$#739296$v$, $v$blue$v$, array[$v$blue$v$,$v$white$v$]::text[], $v$matte$v$, null, 5, 10, true, $v$Cone 6: Weathered Blue is designed to produce a blue to white variegation depending on the application. One coat will produce a sky-blue matte finish with little white variegation. Subsequent coats build a white variegation, muting the sky blue. Cone 10: Off-white variation darkens.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw-136-weathered-blue/$v$, $v$Thinned coats produce a sky blue satin finish. Thick applications will increase white variegation. The brushstroke application is visible in the finished results. We recommend applying coats on bisque in different directions (crosshatch). Although the finish appears opaque, surface decoration can be easily seen through the glaze.$v$, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/sw-136.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-matte$v$, $v$SW-137$v$, $v$Storm Gray$v$, $v$mayco-storm-gray$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Storm Gray is designed to produce a medium gray to white variegation depending on application$v$, $v$#8a8e8a$v$, $v$gray$v$, array[$v$gray$v$,$v$white$v$]::text[], $v$matte$v$, null, 5, 10, true, $v$Cone 6 oxidation (larger image): Storm Gray is designed to produce a medium gray to white variegation depending on application. One coat will produce a medium gray matte finish with little white variegation. Subsequent coats build a white variegation, muting the medium gray. Cone 10 reduction (smaller image): Off-white variation darkens. Gray variation turns blue.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw-137-storm-gray/$v$, $v$Thinned coats produce a medium gray satin finish. Thick applications will increase white variegation. Brush stroke application is visible in finished results. We recommend applying coats on bisque in different directions (crosshatch). Although finish appears opaque, surface decoration can be easily seen through glaze.$v$, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/sw-137.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-matte$v$, $v$SW-138$v$, $v$Lemon Meringue$v$, $v$mayco-lemon-meringue$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Lemon Meringue is designed to produce a bright yellow to white variegation depending on application$v$, $v$#c0aa79$v$, $v$yellow$v$, array[$v$yellow$v$,$v$white$v$]::text[], $v$matte$v$, null, 5, 10, true, $v$Cone 6 oxidation (larger image): Lemon Meringue is designed to produce a bright yellow to white variegation depending on application. One coat will produce a bright yellow matte finish with little white variegation. Subsequent coats build a white variegation, muting the yellow. Cone 10 reduction (smaller image): Off-white variation darkens.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw-138-lemon-meringue/$v$, $v$Thinned coats produce a bright yellow satin finish. Thick applications will increase white variegation. Brush stroke application is visible in finished results. We recommend applying coats on bisque in different directions (crosshatch). Although finish appears opaque, surface decoration can be easily seen through glaze.$v$, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/sw-138.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-matte$v$, $v$SW-140$v$, $v$Black Matte$v$, $v$mayco-black-matte$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Black Matte is formulated to produce a smooth matte surface$v$, $v$#292928$v$, $v$black$v$, array[$v$black$v$]::text[], $v$matte$v$, null, 5, 10, true, $v$Cone 6 oxidation (larger image): Black Matte is formulated to produce a smooth matte surface. Light coats will allow clay body characteristics to appear through the glaze (especially on dark and speckled clay bodies). Cone 10 reduction (smaller image): Color darkens.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw-140-black-matte/$v$, $v$A true matte finish at cone 5/6 with no movement. Thicker application, three or more coats, will produce a more opaque finish.$v$, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/sw-140.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-matte$v$, $v$SW-141$v$, $v$White Matte$v$, $v$mayco-white-matte$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$White Matte is formulated to produce a smooth matte surface$v$, $v$#c1beba$v$, $v$white$v$, array[$v$white$v$]::text[], $v$matte$v$, null, 5, 10, true, $v$Cone 6: White Matte is formulated to produce a smooth matte surface. Light coats will allow clay body characteristics to appear through the glaze (especially on dark and speckled clay bodies). Cone 10: No change.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw-141-white-matte/$v$, $v$A true matte finish at cone 5/6 with no movement. Thicker application, three or more coats, will produce a more opaque finish.$v$, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/sw-141.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-matte$v$, $v$SW-142$v$, $v$Gray Matte$v$, $v$mayco-gray-matte$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Gray Matte is formulated to produce a smooth matte surface$v$, $v$#616161$v$, $v$gray$v$, array[$v$gray$v$]::text[], $v$matte$v$, null, 5, 10, true, $v$Cone 6: Gray Matte is formulated to produce a smooth matte surface. Light coats will allow clay body characteristics to appear through the glaze (especially on dark and speckled clay bodies). Cone 10: Color changes to a blue/gray.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw-142-gray-matte/$v$, $v$A true matte finish at cone 5/6 with no movement. Thicker application, three or more coats, will produce a more opaque finish.$v$, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/sw-142.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-classic$v$, $v$SW-143$v$, $v$Abalone$v$, $v$mayco-abalone$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Abalone is formulated to produce a breaking white and mauve semi-gloss glaze$v$, $v$#a3948e$v$, $v$white$v$, array[$v$white$v$]::text[], $v$gloss$v$, null, 5, 10, true, $v$Cone 6 oxidation (larger image): Abalone is formulated to produce a breaking white and mauve semi-gloss glaze. Light applications will produce a more white semi-gloss finish. Use three+ coats to achieve semi-gloss Abalone finish. Clay body characteristics will be visible through this glaze. Cone 10 reduction (smaller image): Color darkens to purple.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw-143-abalone/$v$, null, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/sw-143.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-crystal$v$, $v$SW-146$v$, $v$Aurora Green$v$, $v$mayco-aurora-green$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Aurora Green produces a mottled aqua gloss glaze with light brown and large black crystals$v$, $v$#74806b$v$, $v$green$v$, array[$v$green$v$,$v$brown$v$,$v$black$v$,$v$blue$v$]::text[], $v$gloss$v$, null, 5, 10, true, $v$Cone 6: Aurora Green produces a mottled aqua gloss glaze with light brown and large black crystals. As the crystals melt, bursts of blue and brown will develop. Cone 10: Color changes to a variegated pink/blue/green. Crystals become less pronounced.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw-146-aurora-green/$v$, $v$SW-108 Green Tea is the base glaze. For a lighter crystal effect, you may try applying two coats of SW-108 Green Tea with a third coat of SW-146 Aurora Green. Due to the large sized crystals in Aurora Green they often reside in the bottom of the glaze; be sure to stir well or pour the glaze out onto a plate to make them more accessible. Wood and soda firing results will vary.$v$, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/sw-146.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-crystal$v$, $v$SW-147$v$, $v$Moonscape$v$, $v$mayco-moonscape$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Moonscape is formulated to produce a medium gray to white variegation mottled with black crystals$v$, $v$#747a71$v$, $v$gray$v$, array[$v$gray$v$,$v$white$v$,$v$black$v$]::text[], $v$matte$v$, null, 5, 10, true, $v$Cone 6: Moonscape is formulated to produce a medium gray to white variegation mottled with black crystals. Light coats will produce a matte gray finish with little white variegation and few crystals. Use three or more coats to produce more white variegation and crystals. At cone 5, this glaze will produce a matte sepia finish with little breaking over texture. Cone 10: Off-white variation darkens. Gray variation turns blue. Crystals melt.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw-147-moonscape/$v$, $v$SW-137 Storm Gray is the base glaze. For a lighter crystal effect, you may try applying two coats of SW-137 Storm Gray with a third coat of SW-147 Moonscape.$v$, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/sw-147.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-crystal$v$, $v$SW-148$v$, $v$Lime Shower$v$, $v$mayco-lime-shower$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Lime Shower is formulated to produce a vibrant chartreuse gloss glaze with dark green and white crystals$v$, $v$#999a5c$v$, $v$green$v$, array[$v$green$v$,$v$white$v$]::text[], $v$gloss$v$, $v$transparent$v$, 5, 10, true, $v$Cone 6 oxidation (larger image): Lime Shower is formulated to produce a vibrant chartreuse gloss glaze with dark green and white crystals. Light coats will produce a semi-transparent finish in the base glaze with fewer crystals. Use three or more coats to produce an opaque green float with more saturation of crystals. At cone 5, this glaze will produce a matte sepia finish with little breaking over texture. Cone 10 reduction (smaller image): Color becomes less vibrant. Crystals melt.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw-148-lime-shower/$v$, $v$SW-253 Green Opal is the base glaze. For a lighter crystal effect, you may try applying two coats of SW-253 Green Opal with a third coat of SW-148 Lime Shower.$v$, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/sw-148.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-crystal$v$, $v$SW-150$v$, $v$Celadon Bloom$v$, $v$mayco-celadon-bloom$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Celadon Bloom is a turquoise semi-transparent gloss glaze that contains a white crystal$v$, $v$#8b978d$v$, $v$celadon$v$, array[$v$celadon$v$,$v$turquoise$v$,$v$white$v$]::text[], $v$gloss$v$, $v$transparent$v$, 5, 10, true, $v$Cone 6 oxidation (larger image): Celadon Bloom is a turquoise semi-transparent gloss glaze that contains a white crystal. Cone 10 reduction (smaller image): Color lightens. Crystals remain.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw-150-celadon-bloom/$v$, $v$SW-201 Turquoise is the base glaze. For a lighter crystal effect, you may try applying two coats of SW-201 Turquoise with a third coat of SW-150 Celadon Bloom.$v$, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/sw-150.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-crystal$v$, $v$SW-151$v$, $v$Olive Float$v$, $v$mayco-olive-float$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Olive Float is a dark green gloss glaze that contains a light green crystal$v$, $v$#3e503b$v$, $v$olive$v$, array[$v$olive$v$,$v$green$v$]::text[], $v$gloss$v$, null, 5, 10, true, $v$Cone 6 oxidation (larger image): Olive Float is a dark green gloss glaze that contains a light green crystal. It is a dazzling glaze that mimics crystalline glazes without the fuss of complicated kiln programing! Cone 10 reduction (smaller image): Color changes to red. Crystals remain.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw-151-olive-float/$v$, $v$SW-210 Emerald is the base glaze. For a lighter crystal effect, you may try applying two coats of SW-210 Emerald with a third coat of SW-151 Olive Float.$v$, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/sw-151.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-crystal$v$, $v$SW-152$v$, $v$Blue Splatterware$v$, $v$mayco-blue-splatterware$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Blue Splatterware is a white, semi-matte glaze that contains a blue crystal$v$, $v$#a4a9b3$v$, $v$blue$v$, array[$v$blue$v$,$v$white$v$]::text[], $v$satin$v$, null, 5, 10, true, $v$Cone 6: Blue Splatterware is a white, semi-matte glaze that contains a blue crystal. As the crystal melts it creates small blue blooms that cause the glaze to resemble the look of 19th century enamelware. Cone 10: Crystals become less defined.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw-152-blue-splatterware/$v$, $v$SW-141 White Matte is the base glaze. For a lighter crystal effect, you may try applying two coats of SW-141 White Matte with a third coat of SW-152 Blue Splatterware.$v$, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/sw-152.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-crystal$v$, $v$SW-153$v$, $v$Indigo Rain$v$, $v$mayco-indigo-rain$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Indigo Rain is a matte white glaze that contains a two-toned purple and violet crystal$v$, $v$#d6cfbe$v$, $v$indigo$v$, array[$v$indigo$v$,$v$white$v$,$v$purple$v$]::text[], $v$matte$v$, null, 5, 10, true, $v$Cone 6: Indigo Rain is a matte white glaze that contains a two-toned purple and violet crystal. As the crystal melts, a purple crystal with violet specks appears. The glaze has a soft subtle beauty. Cone 10: Color darkens to variegated light gray/purple. Crystals melt.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw-153-indigo-rain/$v$, $v$SW-106 Alabaster is the base glaze. For a lighter crystal effect, you may try applying two coats of SW-106 Alabaster with a third coat of SW-153 Indigo Rain.$v$, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/10/SW-153-Indigo-Rain.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-crystal$v$, $v$SW-154$v$, $v$Shipwreck$v$, $v$mayco-shipwreck$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Shipwreck is an aquamarine gloss glaze that contains an iron crystal$v$, $v$#323c38$v$, null, '{}'::text[], $v$gloss$v$, null, 5, 10, true, $v$Cone 6: Shipwreck is an aquamarine gloss glaze that contains an iron crystal. As the crystal melts, a small iron speck appears. The glaze appears mysterious like underwater footage. Cone 10: Color darkens.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw-154-shipwreck/$v$, $v$SW-212 Peacock is the base glaze.For a lighter crystal effect, you may try applying two coats of SW-212 Peacock with a third coat of SW-54 Shipwreck.$v$, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/sw-154.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-crystal$v$, $v$SW-155$v$, $v$Winter Wood$v$, $v$mayco-winter-wood$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Winter Wood is a matte white glaze that contains a variety of brown crystals that melt$v$, $v$#b7a68e$v$, $v$white$v$, array[$v$white$v$,$v$brown$v$]::text[], $v$matte$v$, null, 5, 10, true, $v$Cone 6 oxidation (larger image): Winter Wood is a matte white glaze that contains a variety of brown crystals that melt. Cone 10 reduction (smaller image): Color changes to a translucent golden brown.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw-155-winter-wood/$v$, $v$SW-106 Alabaster is the base glaze. For a lighter crystal effect, you may try applying two coats of SW-106 Alabaster with a third coat of SW-155 Winter Wood.$v$, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/10/SW-155-Winter-Wood-1024x1024.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-crystal$v$, $v$SW-156$v$, $v$Galaxy$v$, $v$mayco-galaxy$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Galaxy is a semi-transparent charcoal colored gloss glaze that contains a three-tone white, orange, and blue crystal$v$, $v$#756a69$v$, $v$white$v$, array[$v$white$v$,$v$orange$v$,$v$blue$v$]::text[], $v$gloss$v$, $v$transparent$v$, 5, 10, true, $v$Cone 6 oxidation (larger image): Galaxy is a semi-transparent charcoal colored gloss glaze that contains a three-tone white, orange, and blue crystal. As the crystal melts, a brilliant bloom of white, orange, and blue appears. The glaze is reminiscent of a star being born. Cone 10 reduction (smaller image): Crystals and base showcase more blue hues. Crystals melt.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw-156-galaxy/$v$, $v$SW-209 Charcoal is the base glaze. For a lighter crystal effect, you may try applying two coats of SW-209 Charcoal with a third coat of SW-156 Galaxy.$v$, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/sw-156.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-matte$v$, $v$SW-158$v$, $v$Lilac Matte$v$, $v$mayco-lilac-matte$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Lilac Matte is a semi-opaque matte lilac glaze$v$, $v$#a27e8b$v$, $v$purple$v$, array[$v$purple$v$]::text[], $v$matte$v$, $v$semi-opaque$v$, 5, 10, true, $v$Cone 6: Lilac Matte is a semi-opaque matte lilac glaze. The glaze will break over surface textures: the more pronounced the surface texture, the more the glaze will pool around these textures. The glaze will create darker areas where it pools. Cone 10: Changes to a translucent gloss.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw-158-lilac-matte/$v$, $v$Lighter coatings will allow body characteristics to appear through the glaze (especially on dark and speckled clay bodies). Thicker application, three or more coats, will produce a more opaque finish.$v$, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/sw-158.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-matte$v$, $v$SW-162$v$, $v$Pink Matte$v$, $v$mayco-pink-matte$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Pink Matte is a semi-opaque matte pink glaze$v$, $v$#bd7569$v$, $v$pink$v$, array[$v$pink$v$]::text[], $v$matte$v$, $v$semi-opaque$v$, 5, 10, true, $v$Cone 6 oxidation (larger image): Pink Matte is a semi-opaque matte pink glaze. Lighter coatings will allow body characteristics to appear through the glaze (especially on dark and speckled clay bodies). Cone 10 reduction (smaller image): Changes to a soft pink translucent gloss.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw-162-pink-matte/$v$, $v$Lighter coatings will allow body characteristics to appear through the glaze (especially on dark and speckled clay bodies). Thicker application, three or more coats, will produce a more opaque finish.$v$, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/sw-162.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-matte$v$, $v$SW-164$v$, $v$Satin Patina$v$, $v$mayco-satin-patina$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Satin Patina is a rich tonal matte green patina glaze$v$, $v$#4d7f71$v$, $v$green$v$, array[$v$green$v$]::text[], $v$satin$v$, $v$opaque$v$, 5, 10, false, $v$Cone 6: Satin Patina is a rich tonal matte green patina glaze. The variation of the glaze is dependent on application. The thicker the application the more opaque and homogenous the color will be, and thinner application will allow more of the clay body to show through the glaze. Satin Patina is a stable glaze. Cone 10: Finish flattens. Color lightens. Brown/orange undertones come through. Note: Not recommended for dinnerware due to surface durability.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw-164-satin-patina/$v$, null, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/sw-164.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-classic$v$, $v$SW-165$v$, $v$Lavender Mist$v$, $v$mayco-lavender-mist$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Lavender Mist is a semi-opaque gloss glaze that displays shades of lavender and brown$v$, $v$#7d646e$v$, $v$brown$v$, array[$v$brown$v$]::text[], $v$gloss$v$, $v$semi-opaque$v$, 5, 10, true, $v$Cone 6: Lavender Mist is a semi-opaque gloss glaze that displays shades of lavender and brown. The variation of the glaze is dependent on application; Thicker application will result in a more opaque and homogenous color. Cone 10: Color darkens.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw-165-lavender-mist/$v$, null, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/sw-165.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-classic$v$, $v$SW-166$v$, $v$Norse Blue$v$, $v$mayco-norse-blue$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Norse Blue is a semi-opaque blue gloss glaze that displays shades of light blue and green$v$, $v$#608b94$v$, $v$blue$v$, array[$v$blue$v$,$v$green$v$]::text[], $v$gloss$v$, $v$semi-opaque$v$, 5, 10, true, $v$Cone 6 oxidation (larger image): Norse Blue is a semi-opaque blue gloss glaze that displays shades of light blue and green. The variation of glaze depends on application. The thicker the application, the more homogenous the color will be. The glaze will break translucent where thinner and pool darker around surface textures. Cone 10 reduction (smaller image): Color darkens.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw-166-norse-blue/$v$, null, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/sw-166.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-classic$v$, $v$SW-167$v$, $v$Sand & Sea$v$, $v$mayco-sand-sea$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Sand & Sea is a semi-opaque gloss glaze that displays shades of light green and gold$v$, $v$#949580$v$, $v$green$v$, array[$v$green$v$,$v$gold$v$]::text[], $v$gloss$v$, $v$semi-opaque$v$, 5, 10, true, $v$Cone 6 oxidation (larger image): Sand & Sea is a semi-opaque gloss glaze that displays shades of light green and gold. The variation of glaze depends on application. The thicker the application, the more homogenous the color will be. The glaze will break translucent where thinner and pool darker around surface textures. Cone 10 reduction (smaller image): Color changes to cream/gray/brown.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw-167-sand-sea/$v$, null, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/sw-167.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-classic$v$, $v$SW-168$v$, $v$Coral Sands$v$, $v$mayco-coral-sands$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Coral Sands is a semi-opaque gloss glaze that displays shades of orange, yellow, and pink$v$, $v$#c18169$v$, $v$pink$v$, array[$v$pink$v$,$v$orange$v$,$v$yellow$v$]::text[], $v$gloss$v$, $v$semi-opaque$v$, 5, 10, true, $v$Cone 6 oxidation (larger image): Coral Sands is a semi-opaque gloss glaze that displays shades of orange, yellow, and pink. The variation of glaze depends on application. The thicker the application, the more homogenous the color will be. The glaze will break translucent where thinner and pool darker around surface textures. Cone 10 reduction (smaller image): Color changes to pink/brown.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw-168-coral-sands/$v$, null, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/sw-168.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-classic$v$, $v$SW-169$v$, $v$Frosted Lemon$v$, $v$mayco-frosted-lemon$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Frosted Lemon is a semi-opaque gloss yellow glaze that displays shades of yellow and white$v$, $v$#b7b089$v$, $v$yellow$v$, array[$v$yellow$v$,$v$white$v$]::text[], $v$gloss$v$, $v$semi-opaque$v$, 5, 10, true, $v$Cone 6: Frosted Lemon is a semi-opaque gloss yellow glaze that displays shades of yellow and white. The variation of glaze depends on application. The thicker the application, the more homogenous the color will be. The glaze will break translucent where thinner and pool darker around surface textures. Cone 10: Color changes to a light pink/purple.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw-169-frosted-lemon/$v$, null, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/sw-169.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-crystal$v$, $v$SW-170$v$, $v$Blue Hydrangea$v$, $v$mayco-blue-hydrangea$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Blue Hydrangea is a blue floral-inspired glaze that contains yellow and white crystals$v$, $v$#5f6370$v$, $v$blue$v$, array[$v$blue$v$,$v$yellow$v$,$v$white$v$]::text[], null, null, 5, 10, true, $v$Cone 6: Blue Hydrangea is a blue floral-inspired glaze that contains yellow and white crystals. As the crystals melt, large white blooms and smaller yellow blooms appear in the glaze. Cone 10: Color changes to blue. Crystals fade slightly.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw-170-blue-hydrangea/$v$, null, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/sw-170.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-crystal$v$, $v$SW-171$v$, $v$Enchanted Forest$v$, $v$mayco-enchanted-forest$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Enchanted Forest is a dark charcoal gloss glaze that contains small yellow and medium-sized green crystals$v$, $v$#4b4740$v$, $v$yellow$v$, array[$v$yellow$v$,$v$green$v$]::text[], $v$gloss$v$, null, 5, 10, true, $v$Cone 6: Enchanted Forest is a dark charcoal gloss glaze that contains small yellow and medium-sized green crystals. As the crystals melt, a variety of yellow and green blooms appear. Cone 10: Base glaze turns dark blue, yellow crystals turn white and green crystals turn blue.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw-171-enchanted-forest/$v$, null, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/sw-171.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-matte$v$, $v$SW-172$v$, $v$Macadamia$v$, $v$mayco-macadamia$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Macadamia is a creamy vanilla matte glaze that adds accents of gold$v$, $v$#948874$v$, $v$gold$v$, array[$v$gold$v$]::text[], $v$matte$v$, null, 5, 10, true, $v$Cone 6 oxidation (larger image): Macadamia is a creamy vanilla matte glaze that adds accents of gold. We recommend firing our matte glazes to cone 6 to produce a satin matte finish. Cone 10 reduction (smaller image): Color changes to a variegated gray/cream. Glossy blue becomes more prominent.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw-172-macadamia/$v$, $v$The variation of the glaze is dependent on application; Thicker application will result in a more homogenous color. The glaze will break over texture and can pool a glossy blue. Wood and soda firing results will vary.$v$, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/sw-172.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-matte$v$, $v$SW-173$v$, $v$Amber Quartz$v$, $v$mayco-amber-quartz$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Amber Quartz is a warm amber matte glaze that adds accents of tan and brown$v$, $v$#70522f$v$, $v$amber$v$, array[$v$amber$v$,$v$tan$v$,$v$brown$v$]::text[], $v$matte$v$, $v$translucent$v$, 5, 10, true, $v$Cone 6 oxidation (larger image): Amber Quartz is a warm amber matte glaze that adds accents of tan and brown. The variation of the glaze is dependent on application. The thicker the application, the more homogenous the color will be. The glaze will break translucent where thinner and pool darker around surface textures. Cone 10 reduction (smaller image): Glossy purple/blue is more prominent. Wood and soda firing results will vary.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw-173-amber-quartz/$v$, null, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/sw-173.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-matte$v$, $v$SW-174$v$, $v$Leather$v$, $v$mayco-leather$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Leather is a matte brown glaze that displays shades of blue and green$v$, $v$#544539$v$, $v$brown$v$, array[$v$brown$v$,$v$blue$v$,$v$green$v$]::text[], $v$matte$v$, $v$translucent$v$, 5, 10, true, $v$Cone 6 oxidation (larger image): Leather is a matte brown glaze that displays shades of blue and green. The variation of the glaze is dependent on application. The thicker the application, the more homogenous the color will be. The glaze will break translucent where thinner and pool darker around surface textures. Cone 10 reduction (smaller image): Glossy blue becomes more prominent.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw-174-leather/$v$, null, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/sw-174.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-matte$v$, $v$SW-175$v$, $v$Rusted Iron$v$, $v$mayco-rusted-iron$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Rusted Iron is a semi-matte, opaque glaze that displays shades of metallic orange and brown$v$, $v$#32251d$v$, $v$orange$v$, array[$v$orange$v$,$v$brown$v$]::text[], $v$metallic$v$, $v$opaque$v$, 5, 10, true, $v$Cone 6: Rusted Iron is a semi-matte, opaque glaze that displays shades of metallic orange and brown. The variation of the glaze is dependent on application. Thicker application results in metallic matte characteristics. Thinner application results in a smoother surface and darker color. Cone 10: Increased orange/copper mottling. Increased movement.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw-175-rusted-iron/$v$, $v$This glaze WILL move. Take care when using on a vertical piece – reduce glaze thickness towards the bottom third to minimize run-off. Over application can cause pinholing or running. Wood and soda firing results will vary.$v$, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/sw-175.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-crystal$v$, $v$SW-176$v$, $v$Sandstone$v$, $v$mayco-sandstone$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Sandstone is a matte, off-white glaze that contains a variety of brown crystals that melt during the firing$v$, $v$#a29681$v$, $v$white$v$, array[$v$white$v$,$v$brown$v$]::text[], $v$matte$v$, null, 5, 10, true, $v$Cone 6: Sandstone is a matte, off-white glaze that contains a variety of brown crystals that melt during the firing. Thicker application and heavy crystal concentration will produce more glossy blue/purple variation. Cone 10: Color darkens. Glossy blue/purples become more prominent.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw-176-sandstone/$v$, $v$SW-172 Macadamia is the base glaze. For a lighter crystal effect, you may try applying two coats of SW-172 Macadamia with a third coat of SW-176 Sandstone. Wood and soda firing results will vary.$v$, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/sw-176.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-classic$v$, $v$SW-177$v$, $v$Raspberry Mist$v$, $v$mayco-raspberry-mist$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Raspberry Mist is a gloss, semi-opaque glaze that displays shades of dark and light pink$v$, $v$#8f4d51$v$, $v$pink$v$, array[$v$pink$v$]::text[], $v$gloss$v$, $v$semi-opaque$v$, 5, 10, true, $v$Cone 6 oxidation (larger image): Raspberry Mist is a gloss, semi-opaque glaze that displays shades of dark and light pink. The variation of glaze depends on application. The thicker the application, the more homogenous the color will be. The glaze will break translucent and appear brighter with thinner application. Cone 10 reduction (smaller image): Color darkens to a deep red.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw-177-raspberry-mist/$v$, $v$Over application of Raspberry Mist can cause pinholing. Brighter color and less variation at cone 5. Wood and soda firing results will vary.$v$, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/sw-177.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-classic$v$, $v$SW-178$v$, $v$Fool's Gold$v$, $v$mayco-fool-s-gold$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Fool’s Gold is a gloss, semi-transparent glaze consisting of a rich brown base with tiny, gold metallic flecks$v$, $v$#20150e$v$, $v$gold$v$, array[$v$gold$v$,$v$brown$v$]::text[], $v$metallic$v$, $v$translucent$v$, 5, 10, true, $v$Cone 6 oxidation (larger image): Fool’s Gold is a gloss, semi-transparent glaze consisting of a rich brown base with tiny, gold metallic flecks. The variation of glaze depends on application. The thicker the application, the more homogenous the color will be. The glaze will break translucent and pool darker around surface textures. Cone 10 reduction (smaller image): Color darkens and produces metallic mottling.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw-178-fools-gold/$v$, null, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/sw-178.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-crystal$v$, $v$SW-179$v$, $v$Muddy Waters$v$, $v$mayco-muddy-waters$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Muddy Waters is a matte brown glaze with crystals that melt into a glossy blue$v$, $v$#7d7158$v$, $v$brown$v$, array[$v$brown$v$,$v$blue$v$]::text[], $v$matte$v$, null, 5, 10, true, $v$Cone 6 oxidation (larger image): Muddy Waters is a matte brown glaze with crystals that melt into a glossy blue. Heavier crystal application will produce more color variation. Cone 10 reduction (smaller image): Glossy blue becomes more prominent. Increased movement.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw-179-muddy-waters/$v$, $v$SW-174 Leather is the base glaze. For a lighter crystal effect, you may try applying two coats of SW-174 Leather with a third coat of SW-179 Muddy Waters. Wood and soda firing results will vary.$v$, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/sw-179.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-crystal$v$, $v$SW-180$v$, $v$Desert Dusk$v$, $v$mayco-desert-dusk$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Desert Dusk is a warm amber matte glaze with crystals that melt into a glossy purple and blue$v$, $v$#c59b66$v$, $v$amber$v$, array[$v$amber$v$,$v$purple$v$,$v$blue$v$]::text[], $v$matte$v$, null, 5, 10, true, $v$Cone 6: Desert Dusk is a warm amber matte glaze with crystals that melt into a glossy purple and blue. Heavier crystal application will produce more color variation. Cone 10: Glossy purple/blue is more prominent. Increased movement.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw-180-desert-dusk/$v$, $v$SW-173 Amber Quartz is the base glaze. For a lighter crystal effect, you may try applying two coats of SW-173 Amber Quartz with a third coat of SW-180 Desert Dusk. Wood and soda firing results will vary.$v$, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/sw-180.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-crystal$v$, $v$SW-181$v$, $v$Night Moth$v$, $v$mayco-night-moth$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Night Moth is an opaque gloss glaze with crystals that bloom into sage and gray$v$, $v$#0f0f11$v$, $v$sage$v$, array[$v$sage$v$,$v$gray$v$]::text[], $v$gloss$v$, $v$opaque$v$, 5, 10, true, $v$Cone 6: Night Moth is an opaque gloss glaze with crystals that bloom into sage and gray. Cone 10: No change.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw-181-night-moth/$v$, $v$SW-508 Black Gloss is the base glaze. For a lighter crystal effect, you may try applying two coats of SW-508 Black Gloss with a third coat of SW-181 Night Moth.$v$, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/sw-181.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-matte$v$, $v$SW-182$v$, $v$Antique Brass$v$, $v$mayco-antique-brass$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Antique Brass is a soft matte, metallic brass glaze that breaks charcoal$v$, $v$#504031$v$, null, '{}'::text[], $v$metallic$v$, null, 5, 10, false, $v$Cone 6 oxidation (larger image): Antique Brass is a soft matte, metallic brass glaze that breaks charcoal. Cone 10 reduction (smaller image): Brass finish becomes brighter and more metallic. Increased movement. Note: Not recommended for dinnerware due to surface durability.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw-182-antique-brass/$v$, null, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/sw-182.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-classic$v$, $v$SW-183$v$, $v$Oxblood$v$, $v$mayco-oxblood$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Oxblood is a milky gloss and transparent glaze that pools red$v$, $v$#c09584$v$, $v$red$v$, array[$v$red$v$]::text[], $v$gloss$v$, $v$transparent$v$, 5, 10, true, $v$Cone 6 oxidation (larger image): Oxblood is a milky gloss and transparent glaze that pools red. Heavier application will produce more red. Cone 10 reduction (smaller image): Gloss finish is enhanced and less milky. Red pooling is brighter.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw-183-oxblood/$v$, $v$Must be applied thick for red variation to appear. Wood and soda firing results will vary.$v$, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/10/SW-183-Oxblood-1024x1024.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-classic$v$, $v$SW-184$v$, $v$Speckled Toad$v$, $v$mayco-speckled-toad$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Speckled Toad is a shimmery green with dark grey specks that bloom when fired$v$, $v$#494734$v$, $v$green$v$, array[$v$green$v$,$v$gray$v$,$v$olive$v$]::text[], null, null, 5, 10, true, $v$Cone 6 oxidation (larger image): Speckled Toad is a shimmery green with dark grey specks that bloom when fired. Glaze breaks a semi-transparant olive green. Cone 10 reduction (smaller image): Color changes to olive green/metallic gray that breaks blue.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw-184-speckled-toad/$v$, null, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/sw-184.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-matte$v$, $v$SW-185$v$, $v$Rainforest$v$, $v$mayco-rainforest$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Rainforest is a soft matte, emerald green glaze that will pool dark and glossy and break a light brown$v$, $v$#505d47$v$, $v$green$v$, array[$v$green$v$,$v$brown$v$]::text[], $v$matte$v$, null, 5, 10, false, $v$Cone 6 oxidation (larger image): Rainforest is a soft matte, emerald green glaze that will pool dark and glossy and break a light brown. Cone 10 reduction (smaller image): Color changes to light brown with green variation where thick/pooling. Increased movement.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw-185-rainforest/$v$, $v$This glaze can be very mobile; Recede coats to avoid run off on vertical pieces and practice caution in combination. Note: Not recommended for dinnerware due to surface durability.$v$, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/03/SW-185.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-matte$v$, $v$SW-186$v$, $v$Azurite$v$, $v$mayco-azurite$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Azurite is a soft matte, cobalt blue glaze that will pool dark and glossy and break a light brown$v$, $v$#33374e$v$, $v$blue$v$, array[$v$blue$v$,$v$brown$v$]::text[], $v$matte$v$, null, 5, 10, false, $v$Cone 6 oxidation (larger image): Azurite is a soft matte, cobalt blue glaze that will pool dark and glossy and break a light brown. Cone 10 reduction (smaller image): Color changes to green where thin/breaking and remains dark blue where thick/pooling. Increased movement.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw-186-azurite/$v$, $v$This glaze can be very mobile; Recede coats to avoid run off on vertical pieces and practice caution in combination. Note: Not recommended for dinnerware due to surface durability. Wood and soda firing results will vary.$v$, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/03/SW-186.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-matte$v$, $v$SW-187$v$, $v$Himalayan Salt$v$, $v$mayco-himalayan-salt$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Himalayan Salt is a soft matte glaze with light pink and burnt orange mottling that will pool a glossy clear$v$, $v$#d4c9b9$v$, $v$pink$v$, array[$v$pink$v$,$v$orange$v$,$v$clear$v$]::text[], $v$matte$v$, null, 5, 10, false, $v$Cone 6: Himalayan Salt is a soft matte glaze with light pink and burnt orange mottling that will pool a glossy clear. Cone 10: Color changes to an opaque, variegated gray/white that breaks gray over texture and can pool a glossy purple/blue when thick.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw-187-himalayan-salt/$v$, $v$This glaze can be very mobile; Recede coats to avoid run off on vertical pieces and practice caution in combination. Note: Not recommended for dinnerware due to surface durability. Wood and soda firing results will vary.$v$, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/03/SW-187.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-crystal$v$, $v$SW-189$v$, $v$Cenote$v$, $v$mayco-cenote$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Cenote is a semi-opaque, sky blue gloss glaze that has a variety of brown crystals that melt during firing$v$, $v$#879e99$v$, $v$blue$v$, array[$v$blue$v$,$v$brown$v$]::text[], $v$gloss$v$, $v$semi-opaque$v$, 5, 10, true, $v$Cone 6: Cenote is a semi-opaque, sky blue gloss glaze that has a variety of brown crystals that melt during firing. Cone 10: Base color darkens. Crystals become darker and more defined.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw-189-cenote/$v$, $v$SW-166 Norse Blue is the base glaze. For a lighter crystal effect, you may try applying two coats of SW-166 Norse Blue with a third coat of SW-189 Cenote. Wood and soda firing results will vary.$v$, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/03/SW-189.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-crystal$v$, $v$SW-191$v$, $v$Peppered Plum$v$, $v$mayco-peppered-plum$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Peppered Plum is a glossy, opaque, burgundy glaze that breaks over texture and develops a warm taupe float; small opaque black crystals are$v$, $v$#733c27$v$, $v$plum$v$, array[$v$plum$v$,$v$burgundy$v$,$v$black$v$]::text[], $v$gloss$v$, $v$transparent$v$, 5, 10, true, $v$Cone 6 oxidation (large photo): Peppered Plum is a glossy, opaque, burgundy glaze that breaks over texture and develops a warm taupe float; small opaque black crystals are featured with large semi-transparent burgundy crystals. Cone 10 reduction (small photo): Glaze darkens, and crystals soften. Large crystal shifts to opaque red. Light application recommended.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw-191-peppered-plum/$v$, $v$SW-113 Speckled Plum is the base glaze. For a lighter crystal effect, apply 1 coat of SW-191 Peppered Plum over 2 coats of SW-113 Speckled Plum. This glaze is stable, even with heavy application. Light application will result in a more homogenous burgundy. Warm taupe float develops and intensifies with glaze thickness.$v$, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/sw-191.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-crystal$v$, $v$SW-190$v$, $v$Passion Flower$v$, $v$mayco-passion-flower$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Passionflower Purple is a glossy, opaque, deep purple glaze with opaque crystals in varying sizes that bloom into shades of blue, green, and$v$, $v$#503558$v$, $v$purple$v$, array[$v$purple$v$,$v$blue$v$,$v$green$v$,$v$yellow$v$]::text[], $v$gloss$v$, $v$opaque$v$, 5, 10, true, $v$Cone 6 oxidation (large photo): Passionflower Purple is a glossy, opaque, deep purple glaze with opaque crystals in varying sizes that bloom into shades of blue, green, and yellow. Cone 10 reduction (small photo): Glaze shifts to a semi-opaque variegated blue that breaks over texture. Crystals soften and lighten. Glaze remains stable.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw-190-passion-flower/$v$, $v$SW-134 Eggplant is the base glaze. For a lighter crystal effect, apply 1 coat of SW-190 Passionflower Purple over 2 coats of SW-134 Eggplant. This glaze is stable, even with heavy application.$v$, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/sw-190.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-crystal$v$, $v$SW-192$v$, $v$Amaryllis$v$, $v$mayco-amaryllis$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Amaryllis is a glossy, transparent, coral glaze with crystals in varying sizes that bloom into shades of brown, yellow, and orange$v$, $v$#f09263$v$, $v$pink$v$, array[$v$pink$v$,$v$brown$v$,$v$yellow$v$,$v$orange$v$]::text[], $v$gloss$v$, $v$transparent$v$, 5, 10, true, $v$Cone 6 oxidation (large photo): Amaryllis is a glossy, transparent, coral glaze with crystals in varying sizes that bloom into shades of brown, yellow, and orange. Cone 10 reduction (small photo): Glaze fades to a transparent pink. Crystals soften. Glaze remains stable.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw-192-amaryllis/$v$, $v$-SW-205 Coral is the base glaze. For a lighter crystal affect, apply 1 coat of SW-192 Amaryllis over 2 coats of SW-205 Coral. This glaze is stable, even with heavy application.$v$, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/sw-192.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-classic$v$, $v$SW-193$v$, $v$Ivy$v$, $v$mayco-ivy$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Ivy is a glossy, opaque, variegated green glaze with that breaks over texture and has an iridescent sheen$v$, $v$#a7ae82$v$, $v$green$v$, array[$v$green$v$]::text[], $v$gloss$v$, $v$opaque$v$, 5, 10, true, $v$Cone 6 oxidation (large photo): Ivy is a glossy, opaque, variegated green glaze with that breaks over texture and has an iridescent sheen. Green micro-crystallization may develop. Cone 10 reduction (small photo): Glaze shifts to a variegated jade that breaks purple over texture. Micro-crystallization enhances.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw-193-ivy/$v$, $v$This glaze is fluid; Apply receding coats to avoid runoff on vertical pieces and practice caution in combination. Prone to pinholes when fired on manganese clay bodies. Wood and soda firing results will vary.$v$, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/sw-193.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-classic$v$, $v$SW-194$v$, $v$Nimbus$v$, $v$mayco-nimbus$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Nimbus is a glossy, opaque, variegated blue glaze that breaks over texture and has an iridescent sheen$v$, $v$#80878c$v$, $v$blue$v$, array[$v$blue$v$]::text[], $v$gloss$v$, $v$opaque$v$, 5, 10, true, $v$Cone 6 oxidation (large photo): Nimbus is a glossy, opaque, variegated blue glaze that breaks over texture and has an iridescent sheen. Blue micro-crystalization may develop. Cone 10 reduction (small photo): Glaze brightens to a variegated cyan that breaks green/brown over texture.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw-194-nimbus/$v$, $v$This glaze is fluid; Apply receding coats to avoid runoff on vertical pieces and practice caution in combination. Prone to pinholes when fired on manganese clay bodies. Wood and soda firing results will vary.$v$, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/sw-194.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-matte$v$, $v$SW-195$v$, $v$Riptide$v$, $v$mayco-riptide$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$: Riptide is a satin-matte, opaque, variegated turquoise/green glaze that breaks over texture and develops a glossy finish where thick or po$v$, $v$#91a585$v$, $v$turquoise$v$, array[$v$turquoise$v$,$v$green$v$]::text[], $v$satin$v$, $v$opaque$v$, 5, 10, false, $v$Cone 6 oxidation (larger image):: Riptide is a satin-matte, opaque, variegated turquoise/green glaze that breaks over texture and develops a glossy finish where thick or pooling. Cone 10 education (smaller image): Glaze shifts grey with white/turquoise variegation. Glaze remains stable.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw-195-riptide/$v$, $v$This glaze is generally stable. Additional coats or increased application thickness may result in movement. Thin application results in finely variegated color. Variegation is exaggerated with application thickness. We recommend firing our matte glazes to cone 6 to produce a satin matte finish.$v$, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/sw-195.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-classic$v$, $v$SW-196$v$, $v$Sand Dollar$v$, $v$mayco-sand-dollar$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Sand Dollar is a satin, opaque, cream-colored glaze with white and gold mottling$v$, $v$#e2c8a2$v$, $v$cream$v$, array[$v$cream$v$,$v$white$v$,$v$gold$v$]::text[], $v$satin$v$, $v$transparent$v$, 5, 10, true, $v$Cone 6 oxidation (large photo): Sand Dollar is a satin, opaque, cream-colored glaze with white and gold mottling. Breaks glossy transparent over texture. Cone 10 reduction (small photo): Glaze shifts to a glossy, variegated lavender purple with white micro-crystallization. Breaks blue/grey over texture. Enhanced mobility.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw-196-sand-dollar/$v$, $v$This glaze is fluid at 3 coats. Anticipate glaze movement with receded application on vertical surfaces to prevent unwanted running. Wood and soda fire results will vary.$v$, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/sw-196.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-matte$v$, $v$SW-197$v$, $v$Fossil Rock$v$, $v$mayco-fossil-rock$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Geologically inspired with mottled earth tones, Fossil Rock is an opaque, tan, matte glaze that breaks over texture$v$, $v$#c0ab81$v$, $v$tan$v$, array[$v$tan$v$]::text[], $v$matte$v$, $v$opaque$v$, 5, 10, false, $v$Cone 6 oxidation (large photo): Geologically inspired with mottled earth tones, Fossil Rock is an opaque, tan, matte glaze that breaks over texture. Cone 10 reduction (small photo): Glaze shifts ivory with soft gray and warm brown marbling. Breaks slate gray over texture. Glaze remains stable.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw-197-fossil-rock/$v$, $v$This glaze is generally stable at 3 coats. Additional coats or increased application thickness may result in glaze movement. We recommend firing our matte glazes to cone 6 to produce a satin matte finish.$v$, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/sw-197.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-classic$v$, $v$SW-198$v$, $v$Rose Quartz$v$, $v$mayco-rose-quartz$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Rose quartz is a glossy, opaque, variegated pink glaze that breaks over texture$v$, $v$#e0aaa4$v$, $v$pink$v$, array[$v$pink$v$]::text[], $v$gloss$v$, $v$opaque$v$, 5, 10, true, $v$Cone 6 oxidation (large photo): Rose quartz is a glossy, opaque, variegated pink glaze that breaks over texture. Pastel pink micro-crystallization may develop on vertical surfaces. Cone 10 reduction (small photo): Glaze darkens and desaturates to a dusty rose with red and mauve variegation and white micro-crystallization. Breaks mauve grey over texture.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw-198-rose-quartz/$v$, $v$This glaze is fluid; Apply receding coats to avoid run off on vertical pieces and practice caution in combination. Over-application of Rose Quartz can cause surface issues. Thin application results in vibrant pink; light pink variegation develops with additional application. The micro-crystallization effect is enhanced in a rapidly cooling kiln.$v$, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/sw-198.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-crystal$v$, $v$SW-199$v$, $v$Purple Aster$v$, $v$mayco-purple-aster$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Purple Aster is a glossy, semi-opaque lavender glaze that breaks over texture and develops a pale violet frost; deep blue crystals melt into$v$, $v$#ac95a6$v$, $v$purple$v$, array[$v$purple$v$,$v$blue$v$]::text[], $v$gloss$v$, $v$semi-opaque$v$, 5, 10, true, $v$Cone 6: Purple Aster is a glossy, semi-opaque lavender glaze that breaks over texture and develops a pale violet frost; deep blue crystals melt into cascading blossoms of indigo. Cone 10: Color darkens slightly. No change to crystals.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw199-purple-aster/$v$, $v$Purple Aster uses SW165 Lavender Mist as the base glaze. This glaze stable at 3 coats, even with heavy application. Crystals can create movement. Avoid having a heavy concentration of crystals near the bottom of your piece. Can be used in oxidation or reduction firings. Results may vary. The choice of clay body, thickness of application, firing process, and temperature will greatly affect the fired results. Always test your application on your clay body in your kiln environment.$v$, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/SW199.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-classic$v$, $v$SW-201$v$, $v$Turquoise$v$, $v$mayco-turquoise$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Turquoise provides translucent, bluish-green gloss color$v$, $v$#829280$v$, $v$turquoise$v$, array[$v$turquoise$v$,$v$green$v$]::text[], $v$gloss$v$, $v$translucent$v$, 5, 10, true, $v$Cone 6: Turquoise provides translucent, bluish-green gloss color. Designed to provide a hint of color with one coat, deeper color with two to three coats – but remaining translucent. Cone 10: Color fades.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw-201-turquoise/$v$, $v$One coat allows more of the clay body characteristics to appear through the glaze, adding a faint color gloss to the surface. Subsequent coats deepen the turquoise color but at three coats you will still obtain a translucent fired surface. Three+ coats will produce more opacity and less translucency.$v$, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/sw-201.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-classic$v$, $v$SW-203$v$, $v$Root Beer$v$, $v$mayco-root-beer$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Root Beer provides translucent, rich, brown gloss color$v$, $v$#2b0e04$v$, $v$brown$v$, array[$v$brown$v$]::text[], $v$gloss$v$, $v$translucent$v$, 5, 10, true, $v$Cone 6: Root Beer provides translucent, rich, brown gloss color. Designed to provide a hint of color with one coat, deeper color with two to three coats – but remaining translucent. Cone 10: Color darkens.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw-203-root-beer/$v$, $v$One coat allows more of the clay body characteristics to appear through the glaze, adding a faint color gloss to the surface. Subsequent coats deepen the brown color but at three coats you will still obtain a translucent fired surface. Three+ coats will produce more opacity and less translucency. This glaze may have some mobility with thicker applications.$v$, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/sw-203.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-classic$v$, $v$SW-204$v$, $v$Amber Topaz$v$, $v$mayco-amber-topaz$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Amber Topaz provides a translucent, light honey-blonde color$v$, $v$#a07946$v$, $v$amber$v$, array[$v$amber$v$,$v$honey$v$]::text[], null, $v$translucent$v$, 5, 10, true, $v$Cone 6: Amber Topaz provides a translucent, light honey-blonde color. Designed to provide a hint of color with one coat, deeper color with two to three coats – but remaining translucent. Cone 10: Color changes to a transparent brown.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw-204-amber-topaz/$v$, $v$One coat allows more of the clay body characteristics to appear through the glaze, adding a faint color gloss to the surface. Subsequent coats deepen the amber color but at three coats you will still obtain a translucent fired surface. Three+ coats will produce more opacity and less translucency. Heavy application may increase the incidence of crazing.$v$, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/sw-204.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-classic$v$, $v$SW-205$v$, $v$Coral$v$, $v$mayco-coral$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Coral provides a translucent, light coral gloss color$v$, $v$#c58878$v$, $v$pink$v$, array[$v$pink$v$]::text[], $v$gloss$v$, $v$translucent$v$, 5, 10, true, $v$Cone 6 oxidation (larger image): Coral provides a translucent, light coral gloss color. You will produce beautiful color variations with Coral without the glaze running off your ware during firing. Designed to provide a hint of color with one coat, deeper color with two to three coats – but remaining translucent. Cone 10 reduction (smaller image): Color lightens.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw-205-coral/$v$, $v$One coat allows more of the clay body characteristics to appear through the glaze, adding a faint color gloss to the surface. Subsequent coats deepen the coral color but at three coats you will still obtain a translucent fired surface. Four+ coats will produce more opacity and less translucency.$v$, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/sw-205.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-classic$v$, $v$SW-210$v$, $v$Emerald$v$, $v$mayco-emerald$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Emerald provides a translucent green gloss color$v$, $v$#191b15$v$, $v$green$v$, array[$v$green$v$]::text[], $v$gloss$v$, $v$translucent$v$, 5, 10, true, $v$Cone 6: Emerald provides a translucent green gloss color. You will produce beautiful color variations with Emerald without the glaze running off your ware during firing. Designed to provide a hint of color with one coat, deeper color with two to three coats – but remaining translucent. Cone 10: Color changes to red in a heavy reduction.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw-210-emerald/$v$, $v$One coat allows more of the clay body characteristics to appear through the glaze, adding a faint color gloss to the surface. Subsequent coats deepen the green color but at three coats you will still obtain a translucent fired surface. Four+ coats will produce more opacity and less translucency.$v$, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/sw-210.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-classic$v$, $v$SW-211$v$, $v$Glacier Blue$v$, $v$mayco-glacier-blue$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Glacier Blue provides a translucent, light blue gloss color$v$, $v$#688f91$v$, $v$blue$v$, array[$v$blue$v$]::text[], $v$gloss$v$, $v$translucent$v$, 5, 10, true, $v$Cone 6 oxidation (larger image): Glacier Blue provides a translucent, light blue gloss color. You will produce beautiful color variations with Glacier Blue without the glaze running off your ware during firing. Designed to provide a hint of color with one coat, deeper color with two to three coats – but remaining translucent. Cone 10 reduction (smaller image): Color lightens.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw-211-glacier-blue/$v$, $v$One coat allows more of the clay body characteristics to appear through the glaze, adding a faint color gloss to the surface. Subsequent coats deepen the blue color but at three coats you will still obtain a translucent fired surface. Four+ coats will produce more opacity and less translucency.$v$, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/sw-211.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-classic$v$, $v$SW-212$v$, $v$Peacock$v$, $v$mayco-peacock$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Peacock provides a translucent, teal gloss color$v$, $v$#2b4c51$v$, $v$teal$v$, array[$v$teal$v$]::text[], $v$gloss$v$, $v$translucent$v$, 5, 10, true, $v$Cone 6 oxidation (larger image): Peacock provides a translucent, teal gloss color. You will produce beautiful color variations with Peacock without the glaze running off your ware during firing. Designed to provide a hint of color with one coat, deeper color with two to three coats – but remaining translucent. Cone 10 reduction (smaller image): Color lightens.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw-212-peacock/$v$, $v$One coat allows more of the clay body characteristics to appear through the glaze, adding a faint color gloss to the surface. Subsequent coats deepen the teal color but at three coats you will still obtain a translucent fired surface. Four+ coats will produce more opacity and less translucency.$v$, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/sw-212.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-classic$v$, $v$SW-214$v$, $v$Micro Pearl$v$, $v$mayco-micro-pearl$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Micro Pearl is a glossy, semi-opaque white glaze with lilac undertones that breaks over texture$v$, $v$#d8cfc6$v$, $v$white$v$, array[$v$white$v$,$v$purple$v$]::text[], $v$gloss$v$, $v$semi-opaque$v$, 5, 10, true, $v$Cone 6 oxidation (larger image): Micro Pearl is a glossy, semi-opaque white glaze with lilac undertones that breaks over texture. Iridescent micro-crystallization in shades of lilac and pale yellow will develop during the firing process. Cone 10 reduction (smaller image): Glaze darkens to blue, purple and white variegation.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw214-micro-pearl/$v$, $v$T his glaze is stable at 3 coats. Additional coats or increased application thickness may result in movement. We recommend firing our micro glazes to cone 6 oxidation to reach crystalline development. Micro-Pearl achieves a stable, semi-opaque, frosted white result with a pearlescent satin finish when fired to cone 5. Can be used in oxidation or reduction firings. Results may vary. The choice of clay body, thickness of application, firing process, and temperature will greatly affect the fired results. Always test your application on your clay body in your kiln environment. Wood and soda firing results will vary.$v$, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/SW214.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-classic$v$, $v$SW-215$v$, $v$Micro Champagne$v$, $v$mayco-micro-champagne$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Micro Champagne is a glossy, translucent amber glaze with a mauve float that breaks over texture$v$, $v$#c39867$v$, $v$amber$v$, array[$v$amber$v$,$v$gold$v$]::text[], $v$gloss$v$, $v$translucent$v$, 5, 10, false, $v$Cone 6 oxidation (larger image): Micro Champagne is a glossy, translucent amber glaze with a mauve float that breaks over texture. Blooms of shimmering gold micro-crystallization will develop during the firing process. Cone 10 reduction (smaller image): Glaze darkens.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw215-micro-champagne/$v$, $v$This glaze is fluid at 3 coats. Recede application to avoid unwanted runoff. Due to the translucent nature of this product, be aware of your application consistency and thickness to avoid streaky brushstrokes. We recommend firing our micro glazes to cone 6 oxidation to reach crystalline development. Micro Champagne achieves a stable, semi-opaque, golden-amber result that breaks over texture and has a pearlescent satin finish when fired to cone 5. Can be used in oxidation or reduction firings. Results may vary. The choice of clay body, thickness of application, firing process, and temperature will greatly affect the fired results. Always test your application on your clay body in your kiln environment.$v$, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/SW215.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-classic$v$, $v$SW-216$v$, $v$Micro Jade$v$, $v$mayco-micro-jade$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Micro Jade is a glossy, translucent, jade green glaze with a turquoise float that breaks over texture$v$, $v$#8c8856$v$, $v$green$v$, array[$v$green$v$,$v$turquoise$v$,$v$bronze$v$]::text[], $v$gloss$v$, $v$translucent$v$, 5, 10, false, $v$Cone 6 oxidation (larger image): Micro Jade is a glossy, translucent, jade green glaze with a turquoise float that breaks over texture. Blooms of shimmering bronze micro-crystallization will develop during the firing process. Cone 10 reduction (smaller image): Glaze turns to a variegated brown.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw216-micro-jade/$v$, $v$This glaze is fluid at 3 coats. Recede application to avoid unwanted runoff. Due to the translucent nature of this product, be aware of your application consistency and thickness to avoid streaky brushstrokes. We recommend firing our micro glazes to cone 6 oxidation to reach crystalline development. Micro Jade achieves a stable, semi-opaque olive result that breaks over texture and has a pearlescent satin finish when fired to cone 5. Can be used in oxidation or reduction firings. Results may vary. The choice of clay body, thickness of application, firing process, and temperature will greatly affect the fired results. Always test your application on your clay body in your kiln environment.$v$, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/SW216.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-classic$v$, $v$SW-217$v$, $v$Micro Cerulean$v$, $v$mayco-micro-cerulean$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Micro Cerulean is a glossy, translucent, medium blue glaze with an aqua float that breaks over texture$v$, $v$#678e9d$v$, $v$blue$v$, array[$v$blue$v$]::text[], $v$gloss$v$, $v$translucent$v$, 5, 10, false, $v$Cone 6 oxidation (larger image): Micro Cerulean is a glossy, translucent, medium blue glaze with an aqua float that breaks over texture. Blooms of shimmering blue micro-crystallization will develop during the firing process. Cone 10 reduction (smaller image): Glaze turns to a variegated grey/blue.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw217-micro-cerulean/$v$, $v$This glaze is stable at 3 coats. Additional coats or increased application thickness may result in movement. Due to the translucent nature of this product, be aware of your application consistency and thickness to avoid streaky brushstrokes. We recommend firing our micro glazes to cone 6 oxidation to reach crystalline development. Micro Cerulean achieves a stable, semi-opaque, deep blue result that breaks over texture and has a pearlescent satin finish when fired to cone 5. Can be used in oxidation or reduction firings. Results may vary. The choice of clay body, thickness of application, firing process, and temperature will greatly affect the fired results. Always test your application on your clay body in your kiln environment.$v$, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/SW217.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-classic$v$, $v$SW-218$v$, $v$Micro Ash$v$, $v$mayco-micro-ash$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Micro Ash is a glossy, translucent, variegated charcoal glaze with a periwinkle float that breaks over texture$v$, $v$#756349$v$, null, '{}'::text[], $v$gloss$v$, $v$translucent$v$, 5, 10, false, $v$Cone 6 oxidation (larger image): Micro Ash is a glossy, translucent, variegated charcoal glaze with a periwinkle float that breaks over texture. Blooms of shimmering onyx micro-crystallization will develop during the firing process. Cone 10 reduction (smaller image): Glaze darkens.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw218-micro-ash/$v$, $v$This glaze is fluid at 3 coats. Recede application to avoid unwanted runoff. Due to the translucent nature of this product, be aware of your application consistency and thickness to avoid streaky brushstrokes. We recommend firing our micro glazes to cone 6 oxidation to reach crystalline development. Micro Ash achieves a stable, semi-opaque, warm charcoal result that breaks over texture and has a pearlescent satin finish when fired to cone 5. Can be used in oxidation or reduction firings. Results may vary. The choice of clay body, thickness of application, firing process, and temperature will greatly affect the fired results. Always test your application on your clay body in your kiln environment.$v$, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/SW218.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-classic$v$, $v$SW-219$v$, $v$Opal Lustre$v$, $v$mayco-opal-lustre$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Opal Lust re is a glossy, semi-opaque glaze that displays variegated shades of blues, greens, and purples$v$, $v$#a68e72$v$, $v$brown$v$, array[$v$brown$v$]::text[], $v$gloss$v$, $v$semi-opaque$v$, 5, 10, true, $v$Cone 6 oxidation (larger image): Opal Lust re is a glossy, semi-opaque glaze that displays variegated shades of blues, greens, and purples. Breaks warm brown over texture. Cone 10 reduction (smaller image): Color flattens, and warm undertones come through.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw219-opal-lustre/$v$, $v$This glaze is semi-fluid at 3 coats. Additional coats or increased application thickness may result in movement. Can be used in oxidation or reduction firings. Results may vary. The choice of clay body, thickness of application, firing process, and temperature will greatly affect the fired results. Always test your application on your clay body in your kiln environment. Wood and soda firing results will vary.$v$, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/SW219.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-crystal$v$, $v$SW-226$v$, $v$Pink Pearl$v$, $v$mayco-pink-pearl$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Pink Pearl is a glossy, semi-opaque white glaze that breaks over texture$v$, $v$#e3bab9$v$, $v$pink$v$, array[$v$pink$v$,$v$white$v$]::text[], $v$gloss$v$, $v$semi-opaque$v$, 5, 10, false, $v$Cone 6: Pink Pearl is a glossy, semi-opaque white glaze that breaks over texture. Contains pink crystals. Base color is stable, crystals can create movement. Cone 10: Pink Pearl changes to a glossy blue. Heavy crystal application may effect color results and movement.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw226-pink-pearl/$v$, $v$Pink Pearl uses SW223 Milk Glass as the base. Upon opening, crystals will be concentrated in the bottom of the bottle. Stir/shake thoroughly to incorporate before each use. Crystals can create movement. Avoid having a heavy concentration of crystals near the bottom of your piece. When storing a crystal glaze, you may consider storing upside down to make crystal more accessible.$v$, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/SW226-Pink-Pearl.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-crystal$v$, $v$SW-227$v$, $v$Tidal Wave$v$, $v$mayco-tidal-wave$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Tidal Wave is a glossy, semi-opaque white glaze that breaks over texture$v$, $v$#a6b0ba$v$, $v$white$v$, array[$v$white$v$,$v$blue$v$]::text[], $v$gloss$v$, $v$semi-opaque$v$, 5, 10, false, $v$Cone 6: Tidal Wave is a glossy, semi-opaque white glaze that breaks over texture. Contains blue crystals. Base color is stable, crystals can create movement. Cone 10: Tidal Wave changes to a glossy blue. Heavy crystal application may effect color results and movement.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw227-tidal-wave/$v$, $v$Tidal Wave uses SW223 Milk Glass as the base. Upon opening, crystals will be concentrated in the bottom of the bottle. Stir/shake thoroughly to incorporate before each use. Crystals can create movement. Avoid having a heavy concentration of crystals near the bottom of your piece. When storing a crystal glaze, you may consider storing upside down to make crystal more accessible.$v$, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/SW227-Tidal-Wave.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-classic$v$, $v$SW-229$v$, $v$Mood Ring$v$, $v$mayco-mood-ring$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Mood Ring is a glossy, opaque dark green glaze that breaks brown over texture and has an iridescent sheen$v$, $v$#424530$v$, $v$green$v$, array[$v$green$v$,$v$brown$v$]::text[], $v$gloss$v$, $v$opaque$v$, 5, 10, false, $v$Cone 6: Mood Ring is a glossy, opaque dark green glaze that breaks brown over texture and has an iridescent sheen. Semi-fluid at 3 coats. Cone 10: Mood Ring darkens. Heavier reduction may produce surface texture.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw229-mood-ring/$v$, null, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/SW229-Mood-Ring.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-classic$v$, $v$SW-228$v$, $v$Beetlewing$v$, $v$mayco-beetlewing$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Beetle Wing is a glossy, opaque green glaze that breaks over texture and has an iridescent sheen$v$, $v$#646845$v$, $v$green$v$, array[$v$green$v$]::text[], $v$gloss$v$, $v$opaque$v$, 5, 10, false, $v$Cone 6: Beetle Wing is a glossy, opaque green glaze that breaks over texture and has an iridescent sheen. Semi-fluid at 3 coats. Cone 10: Beetle Wing changes to a glossy blue.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw228-beetlewing/$v$, null, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/SW228-Beetlewing.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-matte$v$, $v$SW-230$v$, $v$Pink Speck$v$, $v$mayco-pink-speck$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Pink Speck is a satin-matte, semi-opaque light pink glaze that breaks over texture$v$, $v$#f7ab9e$v$, $v$pink$v$, array[$v$pink$v$,$v$purple$v$,$v$orange$v$,$v$yellow$v$]::text[], $v$satin$v$, $v$semi-opaque$v$, 5, 10, true, $v$Cone 6: Pink Speck is a satin-matte, semi-opaque light pink glaze that breaks over texture. Contains small purple, orange and yellow specks. Stable glaze. Cone 10: Pink Speck lightens. Specks blur and lose definition with increased application thickness; crystallization may develop. Remains stable.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw230-pink-speck/$v$, $v$We recommend firing our Pink Speck glaze to cone 6 to produce a satin matte finish. Upon opening, specks will be concentrated in the bottom of the bottle. Stir/shake thoroughly to incorporate before each use.$v$, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/SW230-Pink-Speck.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-classic$v$, $v$SW-250$v$, $v$White Opal$v$, $v$mayco-white-opal$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$White Opal forms a clear- to- milky white gloss surface$v$, $v$#c8c3bd$v$, $v$white$v$, array[$v$white$v$,$v$clear$v$]::text[], $v$gloss$v$, null, 5, 10, true, $v$Cone 6 oxidation (larger image): White Opal forms a clear- to- milky white gloss surface. One coat produces the clearest finish; subsequent layering increases the incidence of a white precipitate forming. Prominent white to bluish-white colors will emerge where the glaze pools and gathers around surface texture. Cone 10 reduction (smaller image): White variation lessens leaving a transparent gloss with white pooling.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw-250-white-opal/$v$, $v$White coloration is more visible on darker clay bodies (Buff, Manganese Speck). Thinner application will provide a glossy transparent finish. Thicker application will provide white floating. Wood and soda firing results will vary.$v$, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/sw-250.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-classic$v$, $v$SW-251$v$, $v$Pink Opal$v$, $v$mayco-pink-opal$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Pink Opal produces a desert rose pink that ranges from semi-translucent to fully opaque, depending on application thickness$v$, $v$#ac6c74$v$, $v$pink$v$, array[$v$pink$v$,$v$clear$v$]::text[], $v$gloss$v$, $v$translucent$v$, 5, 10, true, $v$Cone 6 oxidation (larger image): Pink Opal produces a desert rose pink that ranges from semi-translucent to fully opaque, depending on application thickness. Thin applications yield a clear glaze with hints of pink precipitate; heavier applications will create an opaque purple-pink gloss finish that can also form a whitish cast in select areas. Cone 10 reduction (smaller image): Pink fades out entirely, leaving a transparent gloss with white pooling.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw-251-pink-opal/$v$, $v$Vertical pieces best allow the glaze to flow and create a semi-transparent, rose veil. Body textures and features will still be visible through the glaze. Thinner application will provide a glossy transparent finish. Thicker application will provide light pink floating. Surface decoration will be visible under the glaze, but if you apply the glaze thick, it could blur your image.$v$, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/sw-251.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-classic$v$, $v$SW-252$v$, $v$Blue Opal$v$, $v$mayco-blue-opal$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Blue Opal is a medium blue semi-transparent to fully opaque gloss glaze$v$, $v$#517286$v$, $v$blue$v$, array[$v$blue$v$]::text[], $v$gloss$v$, $v$transparent$v$, 5, 10, true, $v$Cone 6: Blue Opal is a medium blue semi-transparent to fully opaque gloss glaze. Thinner applications create a transparent blue haze; thicker coatings produce an opaque finish. Surface textures can cause the glaze to collect and produce streaks of greyish blue. Cone 10: Becomes more transparent. Can produce red mottling in a heavy reduction.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw-252-blue-opal/$v$, $v$Light applications on brown and buff bodies will produce a transparent green-blue gloss finish. Thinner application will provide a glossy transparent finish. Thicker application will provide light blue floating. Surface decoration will be visible under the glaze, but if you apply the glaze thick, it could blur your image.$v$, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/sw-252.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-classic$v$, $v$SW-253$v$, $v$Green Opal$v$, $v$mayco-green-opal$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Green Opal achieves a vibrant chartreuse gloss when fired$v$, $v$#a7aa63$v$, $v$green$v$, array[$v$green$v$,$v$yellow$v$]::text[], $v$gloss$v$, $v$semi-opaque$v$, 5, 10, true, $v$Cone 6: Green Opal achieves a vibrant chartreuse gloss when fired. Lighter applications lead to a semi-opaque yellow-green; heavier applications see the formation of a green float. Cone 10: Color lightens; becomes more transparent.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw-253-green-opal/$v$, $v$Darker clay bodies, such as buff and brown, display the phosphorescent qualities of Green Opal. On manganese bodies, Green Opal will interact with manganese bodies, creating interesting brown streaks. Thinner application will provide a glossy transparent finish. Thicker application will provide light green floating. Surface decoration will be visible under the glaze, but if you apply the glaze thick, it could blur your image. and pool into$v$, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/sw-253.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-classic$v$, $v$SW-255$v$, $v$Gray Opal$v$, $v$mayco-gray-opal$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Gray Opal creates a transparent gloss finish$v$, $v$#797877$v$, $v$gray$v$, array[$v$gray$v$]::text[], $v$gloss$v$, $v$transparent$v$, 5, 10, true, $v$Cone 6 oxidation (larger image): Gray Opal creates a transparent gloss finish. It deepens in color from one coat to three but surface decoration and design remain visible through theglaze even with three coats. The glaze will break and pool around surface textures, creating opportunities for the opalescent character to develop. Cone 10 reduction (smaller image): Color lightens; becomes more transparent.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw-255-gray-opal/$v$, $v$Thinner application will provide a glossy transparent finish. Thicker application will provide blue white floating. Surface decoration will be visible under the glaze, but if you apply the glaze thick, it could blur your image.$v$, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/sw-255.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
  ($v$mayco$v$, $v$stoneware-gloss$v$, $v$SW-501$v$, $v$White Gloss$v$, $v$mayco-white-gloss$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$White Gloss is a highly-pigmented true white gloss glaze$v$, $v$#e3dfda$v$, $v$white$v$, array[$v$white$v$]::text[], $v$gloss$v$, $v$opaque$v$, 5, 10, true, $v$Cone 6 oxidation (larger image): White Gloss is a highly-pigmented true white gloss glaze. The stable qualities of this glaze make it ideal for design work and full opaque coverage at mid-range temperatures. Cone 10 reduction (smaller image): No change.$v$, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/product/sw-501-white-gloss/$v$, null, null, null, $v$https://www.maycocolors.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/sw-501.jpg$v$, $v$Mayco$v$),
